  "query_preview": "..Infrared imagery showed wrapped around clouds\nacross far SE Cochise county early this morning associated with\na weak upper low that was over NE Sonora MX per water vapor \nimagery. This upper low developed mostly virga yesterday \nafternoon/evening with outflows from the virga producing wind \ngusts of 52 mph at Nogales airport, 45 mph at Pioneer Air Field \nand 43 mph at Tucson Intl airport. The upper low will move east\ntoday into Chihuahua MX with upper ridging building in from the\nwest. Today is the last day of Arizona Heat Awareness Week and \nthe warm-up that occurred yesterday will continue today into the\nweekend with a return to triple-digit highs for the lower \ndeserts. There is some temperature guidance out there that \nshows Sunday (10th) possibly as hot as Monday (11th). \n\nDays 4-7 (Monday May 11th to Thursday May 14th)\nHot on the 11th with record highs from Tucson west with isolated\nareas having HeatRisk in the Major category. See climate section\nbelow for locations near record high. Above normal highs \ncontinue 12th through 14th even with slight cooling. With the \nupper high shifting east on the 12th and 13th, mid-level flow \nturns to the south, which may advect mid- level moisture into \nthe eastern areas. Plenty of uncertainty at how much moisture \nwill be pulled north thus probabilities for measurable rain are \non the very low side. Stay tuned.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (May 15th to 21st)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (42%-50%)\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal east of Tucson (33%-39%)",
